From: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: RDNA1 matrix-vector kernels: parameter table, v_sad_u8 sums, float-activation matvec

The quantized matrix-vector kernel picks its launch geometry from a per-
architecture table that has no RDNA1 entry, so gfx1013 ran the generic one,
four warps per row with a shared-memory exchange and a barrier. RDNA1 also has
no v_dot4, and the emulated int8 dot costs 1.9 times the instructions.

Three parts, all behind RDNA1 checks:
- an RDNA1 entry in the table: one wave per row for the K-quants and IQ types,
  four warps for Q4_0/Q4_1/Q5_0/Q5_1/Q8_0 (whose vec_dot is short and memory-
  bound), and a long-K variant (K >= 8192) that splits the K-quants' reduction
  across four warps again;
- ggml_cuda_sum_i8x4 through v_sad_u8 for the activation sums of the q4_K,
  q5_K and q2_K paths (dp4a with 0x01010101), exact integer arithmetic;
- mmvq-rdna1-f32.cu: a float-activation matvec laid out like ggml-vulkan's
  shaders (16 threads per 256-value superblock, one wave two rows) for q4_K,
  q5_K, q6_K, q8_0, iq2_xxs, iq3_xxs and iq3_s, single column, with MMVQ's
  bias/gate/GLU fusion and the MUL_MAT_ID path for one token, dispatched ahead
  of the q8_1 quantization. iq4_xs was measured and left on the int8 path
  (its byte-permute vec_dot is faster).

test-backend-ops single-column MUL_MAT and MUL_MAT_ID cases match the CPU for
every covered type; perplexity gates are bit-identical (the kernel is single
column and never enters batched prefill); greedy text is token-identical on
the 8B and the MoE and differs at one near-tie token on the 1.5B and 27B.
Decode on a BC-250 against the three-patch build: qwen2.5-1.5B x1.66, the 14B
models x1.5, qwen3.6-35B MoE x2.05, qwen3.8-27B x1.89, the Q8_0 8B unchanged.
logs/rdna1-mmvq-2026-09-18 in the repository.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
